---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, REPORT_FORM_URL } from '../config';

const reportsGoToForm = REPORT_FORM_URL !== '';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description={`${SITE_NAME} has no accounts, no cookies, no analytics and no ads. The only thing stored is your light or dark theme choice, in your own browser.`}
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>This page is short because the site does very little with your data.</p>

      <h2>What the site does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts. There is nothing to sign up for or log in to.</li>
        <li>No cookies.</li>
        <li>No analytics or tracking scripts of any kind.</li>
        <li>No ads in this version of the site.</li>
        <li>No record of which questions you open or how you answer them. A page's "correct" count lives in memory and is gone when you leave the page.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The one thing stored</h2>
      <p>
        If you switch between the light and dark theme, your choice is saved in your browser's localStorage
        under the key <code>theme</code>, so the site looks the same next time. That value never leaves your
        device; clearing the site's data in your browser removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Error reports</h2>
      <p>
        The Report an error link under each question takes you
        {reportsGoToForm ? ' to a report form run by its provider' : ' to GitHub'}. Anything you write
        there is handled by that service under its own privacy policy, not by {SITE_NAME}.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a set of static files served by a hosting provider. {SITE_NAME} itself runs no server
        code and keeps no logs.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
